{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' __issue_context__.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"body\": \"**CL term**\\n[CL_0001057](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0001057) — myeloid dendritic cell, human\\n[CL_0001058](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0001058) — plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\\n\\n**Suggested revision of class hierarchy**\\nAdd: lacks expression of CD14\\nAlthough there were previous attempts to annotate DCs with CD14-negative expression (Issue [#123](https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/123), [#125](https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/125), [#127](https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/127)), these were unfortunately closed without resolution.\\n\\n**textual def**\\nplease add in the textual def that this cell is CD14-negative.\\n\\n**References**  **Add these references but do not replace exisiting references**\\n\\nRelevant OMIP references demonstrating standard gating strategy:\\n1. [OMIP-77](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34260151/)\\n2. [OMIP-87](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36470845/)\\n3. [OMIP-94](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37254600/)\\n4. [OMIP-101](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38343094/)\\n5. [OMIP-112](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40095400/)\\n\\n\\nThese human dendritic cell populations are consistently defined as CD14-negative in flow cytometry gating strategies. Although some tissue-specific DC subsets (e.g., dermal DCs) may express CD14, the general population of human DCs is gated as CD14⁻ to distinguish them from monocytes.\\n\\n\\nThank you for your consideration.\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-87TaXzk\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"KazuhiroNakagawa\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"NONE\",\n      \"body\": \"@dosumis, @addiehl There seems to be no progress since July, I would like to know the status. \",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-18T10:51:20Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3163#issuecomment-3546905828\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-87Yc5s2\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Caroline-99\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n      \"body\": \"@addiehl could you please check this out ? I agree with adding lack CD14 expression to \\\"[CL_0001057](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0001057) — myeloid dendritic cell, human and [CL_0001058](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0001058) — plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\\\". However, I am not sure about adding it to the general human term [CL_0001056](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0001056) — dendritic cell, human as there are some human dendritic cells that do express CD14 (PMID: [23621371](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23621371/), [PMID: 34279540](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8292131/). Thank you \",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-12-09T10:23:05Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3163#issuecomment-3631455030\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"[Class hierarchy] Add \\\"CD14 lacks\\\" to human dendritic cell terms\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3163\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
