=10.1046/j.1523-1747.1998.00162.x&amp;\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Scholar</a>]</li>\n1658-<li id=\"b98\">\n1659:<cite>Kanitakis J, Morelon E, Petruzzo P, Badet L, Dubernard JM. Self-renewal capacity of human epidermal Langerhans cells: observations made on a composite tissue allograft. Exp Dermatol. 2011;20:145–6. doi: 10.1111/j.1600-0625.2010.01146.x.</cite> [<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0625.2010.01146.x\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DOI</a>] [<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20707812/\" class=\"usa-link\">PubMed</a>] [<a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Exp%20Dermatol&amp;title=Self-renewal%20capacity%20of%20human%20epidermal%20Langerhans%20cells:%20observations%20made%20on%20a%20composite%20tissue%20allograft&amp;author=J%20Kanitakis&amp;author=E%20Morelon&amp;author=P%20Petruzzo&amp;author=L%20Badet&amp;author=JM%20Dubernard&amp;volume=20&amp;publication_year=2011&amp;pages=145-6&amp;pmid=20707812&amp;doi=10.1111/j.1600-0625.2010.01146.x&amp;\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Scholar</a>]</li>\n1660-<li id=\"b99\">\n1661:<cite>Strobl H, Riedl E, Scheinecker C, Bello-Fernandez C, Pickl WF, Rappersberger K, Majdic O, Knapp W. TGF-β1 promotes in vitro development of dendritic cells from CD34+ hemopoietic progenitors. J Immunol. 1996;157:1499–507.</cite> [<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8759731/\" class=\"usa-link\">PubMed</a>] [<a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=J%20Immunol&amp;title=TGF-%CE%B21%20promotes%20in%20vitro%20development%20of%20dendritic%20cells%20from%20CD34+%20hemopoietic%20progenitors&amp;author=H%20Strobl&amp;author=E%20Riedl&amp;author=C%20Scheinecker&amp;author=C%20Bello-Fernandez&amp;author=WF%20Pickl&amp;volume=157&amp;publication_year=1996&amp;pages=1499-507&amp;pmid=8759731&amp;\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Scholar</a>]</li>\n1662-<li id=\"b100\">\n1663:<cite>Geissmann F, Prost C, Monnet JP, Dy M, Brousse N, Hermine O. Transforming growth factor β1, in the presence of granulocyte/macrophage colony-stimulating factor and interleukin 4, induces differentiation of human peripheral blood monocytes into dendritic Langerhans cells. J Exp Med. 1998;187:961–6. doi: 10.1084/jem.187.6.961.</cite> [<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1084/jem.187.6.961\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DOI</a>] [<a href=\"/articles/PMC2212193/\" class=\"usa-link\">PMC free article</a>] [<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9500798/\" class=\"usa-link\">PubMed</a>] [<a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=J%20Exp%20Med&amp;title=Transforming%20growth%20factor%20%CE%B21,%20in%20the%20presence%20of%20granulocyte/macrophage%20colony-stimulating%20factor%20and%20interleukin%204,%20induces%20differentiation%20of%20human%20peripheral%20blood%20monocytes%20into%20dendritic%20Langerhans%20cells&amp;author=F%20Geissmann&amp;author=C%20Prost&amp;author=JP%20Monnet&amp;author=M%20Dy&amp;author=N%20Brousse&amp;volume=187&amp;publication_year=1998&amp;pages=961-6&amp;pmid=9500798&amp;doi=10.1084/jem.187.6.961&amp;\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Scholar</a>]</li>\n1664-<li id=\"b101\">\n1665-<cite>Ginhoux F, Tacke F, Angeli V, et al.  Langerhans cells arise from monocytes in vivo. Nat Immunol. 2006;7:265–73. doi: 10.1038/ni1307.</cite> [<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/ni1307\" class=\"usa-link usa-link--external\" data-ga-action=\"click_feat_suppl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener n